e animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s what I thought. Thanks. Is it true that Lazarus was the progenitor of the Lamiae bloodline?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes it was, and for some reason Lazarus decided to resurrect the bloodline for the family reunion (V5). Very suspicious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T10:46:02-08:00","id":1362157,"title":"","content":"Fascinating. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T12:20:54-08:00","id":1362188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1362149-is-the-methuselah-lazarus-the-same-as-the-biblical-lazarus#post1362149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or is he another Cainite with the same name?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it could be that the Lazarus-relevant parts of the anonymous accounts that became the four Gospels were actually about the vampire Lazarus.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T16:35:17-08:00","id":1362266,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> but Lazarus Embraced the founder of the Lamiae, and the Lamiae were around in the Mythic Age of Greece, long before the time of Jesus. Doesn\u2019t that mean that the Methuselah Lazarus can\u2019t possibly be the same Lazarus from the Gospels?<br /> <br /> Not arguing with you. I\u2019m genuinely curious. I love history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T16:38:38-08:00","id":1362267,"title":"","content":"Ohhhhhhh<br /> <br /> I get it!!!<br /> <br /> You mean what if Lazarus from the Gospels was actually a vampire.<br /> <br /> Hmmmm. Maybe.<br /> <br /> I think the beloved disciple from the Gospel of John was actually Mary Magdalen, but I\u2019m not sure if that\u2019s relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T16:55:37-08:00","id":1362271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1362149-is-the-methuselah-lazarus-the-same-as-the-biblical-lazarus?p=1362267#post1362267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean what if Lazarus from the Gospels was actually a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in Vampire: the Masquerade, anyway. It's much more likely that Lazarus from the Gospels was just, like, a dude. Maybe some people mistook him for dead, and Yeshua came by and &quot;resurrected&quot; him with some quick CPR, and in the decades that passed between the time Yeshua the itinerant rabbi was supposedly alive and the time that people bothered to write the oral traditions down, the story got embellished and exaggerated until he'd been dead for three days.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut, y'know, if Lazarus <i>had</i> been a Cainite who'd fallen into torpor and Jesus brought him around again with some blood, that's about as probable as the account in Luke being factually true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T17:04:42-08:00","id":1362273,"title":"","content":"I believe it. I\u2019m not a Christian, but for every action there\u2019s a reaction. For every Goddess there\u2019s a God. I believe that the Abrahamic God exists. He\u2019s just not the god I worship.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Imma go watch The Bachelor. Thanks for helping me figure this out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T17:18:00-08:00","id":1362279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1362149-is-the-methuselah-lazarus-the-same-as-the-biblical-lazarus?p=1362273#post1362273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that the Abrahamic God exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then he's got a lot to answer for; either he's said some absolutely horrible, <i>vile</i> things, or he needs an object lesson in who he lets speak for him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1362149-is-the-methuselah-lazarus-the-same-as-the-biblical-lazarus?p=1362273#post1362273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, Imma go watch The Bachelor. Thanks for helping me figure this out.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T17:32:56-08:00","id":1362285,"title":"","content":"I don't think Lazarus is the Biblical Lazarus, but if he were well, if any of the Antediluvians were going to find the guy who died and was resurrected and turn him into a vampire, I think Cappadocius would be the first in line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T18:15:11-08:00","id":1362291,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> true, but the New Testament isn\u2019t really that bad. Fornication (hooking up) is only criticized once in a laundry list of like twenty other relatively minor sins, while adultery (cheating) is condemned in all four Gospels. Unfortunately, the patriarchy completely distorts what Jesus actually said to the point where it\u2019s totally unrecognizable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T18:29:29-08:00","id":1362294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1362149-is-the-methuselah-lazarus-the-same-as-the-biblical-lazarus?p=1362291#post1362291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">true, but the New Testament isn\u2019t really that bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's where we get the notion of hell <i>in its entirety</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200bWell, that and the Apocalypse of Peter apocrypha.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut point is, before that, Old Testament didn't really have much to say about what happens after you die (you &quot;lie with your fathers&quot;). Moreover, Jesus had every opportunity to take back some of the things his dad said, and <i>didn't</i> - he specifically says that <i>not a jot or a tiddle</i> of the old laws (including the rules about stoning people to death for being gay or having been too traumatized to scream while being raped, the laws defining how you can own humans and the extent to which you can beat the humans you own, or the stricture against menstruating women or people with crushed genitals getting to be around God) will pass away before heaven and earth do.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's also in the New Testament where Paul tells slaves to obey their masters, even the cruel ones; and women to be silent in church, and if they have questions, to talk it out with their husbands after.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1362149-is-the-methuselah-lazarus-the-same-as-the-biblical-lazarus?p=1362291#post1362291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, the patriarchy completely distorts what Jesus actually said to the point where it\u2019s totally unrecognizable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but if your argument is, &quot;We can't even recognize what Jesus actually said because it's so distorted,&quot; then why does it matter if the New Testament is less bad than the Old?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-20-2020, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T18:51:38-08:00","id":1362300,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> my friend is an evangelical minister and he told me that the coming of Jesus abolished all of the old laws except for the Ten Commandments. (Granted, he doesn\u2019t actually know I\u2019m a witch, but still.)<br /> <br /> I agree with you that Christianity is badly flawed. That\u2019s why I\u2019m not Christian. I\u2019m just saying that if you get rid of some of the more extreme passages (the one about menstruating women is pretty bad, but I don\u2019t even know anyone with crushed genitals...), the central tenets of the New Testament (Love thy neighbor) is not that bad.<br /> <br /> If this triggers you for real we don\u2019t have to talk about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T19:02:12-08:00","id":1362305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1362149-is-the-methuselah-lazarus-the-same-as-the-biblical-lazarus?p=1362300#post1362300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my friend is an evangelical minister and he told me that the coming of Jesus abolished all of the old laws except for the Ten Commandments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, because it'd be very convenient for Christians if they didn't have to worry about pissing off the invisible sky-daddy for wearing a poly-fabric shirt or eating at Red Lobster. A lot of them still manage to forget that when it comes to condemning homosexuals, depressingly enough.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, you should ask him sometime why boiling a goat in its mother's milk got into the Ten Commandments, but God couldn't be arsed to have Moses write down &quot;Don't rape, like, at all,&quot; and &quot;Don't own people as property, ya dipshits&quot; and just have a round Dozen Commandments.<br /> <br /> \u200b(And if he doesn't know what you mean by boiling a goat in its mother's milk, that's because those ten rules that Moses carried down Mount Sinai were not explicitly called the Ten Commandments; the version that <i>does</i> get referred to as the Ten Commandments includes that very specific rule.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T19:10:42-08:00","id":1362312,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m part of the LGBTQ community and I absolutely agree with you about rape and slavery, but I\u2019ve read the Ten Commandments and there\u2019s nothing in there about goats. That\u2019s probably one of the kosher dietary laws (although I think they say you CAN\u2019T mix meat and milk, but I\u2019m not 100% sure).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"",